: ["ga", "Ursus americanus", "Alces alces"], "muledeer>blackbear": ["ga", "Ursus americanus", "Odocoileus hemionus"], "beaver>blackbear": ["ga", "Ursus americanus", "Castor canadensis"], "coyote>wolf": ["ga", "Canis lupus", "Canis latrans"], "raven>wolf": ["ga", "Canis lupus", "Corvus corax"], "blackbear>wolf": ["ga", "Canis lupus", "Ursus americanus"], "willow>grizzly": ["ga", "Ursus arctos", "Salix"], "aspen>grizzly": ["ga", "Ursus arctos", "Populus tremuloides"], "muledeer>grizzly": ["ga", "Ursus arctos", "Odocoileus hemionus"], "beaver>grizzly": ["ga", "Ursus arctos", "Castor canadensis"], "coyote>grizzly": ["ga", "Ursus arctos", "Canis latrans"], "blackbear>grizzly": ["ga", "Ursus arctos", "Ursus americanus"]}, "story": "Grand Teton National Park in Wyoming covers about 310,000 acres, including the 40-mile Teton Range and the northern part of Jackson Hole. Over 1,000 vascular plant species, 300 bird species and more than a dozen fish species live here. Some rocks are nearly 2.7 billion years old.", "matters": "It is 10 miles south of Yellowstone, and together with surrounding national forests they form the Greater Yellowstone Ecosystem, one of the largest intact temperate ecosystems."}